Chapter 1

;Life cycle of the hello world program:

1-information is bits + context, 
the program is saved in memory as binary characters
where binary is 0s and 1s
each 0 or 1 is one bit
each 8 bits are grouped together in a byte
the byte is the smallest memory unit you usually deal with
files that consist of ascii characters are called text files
and files of ascii that are code are called source files
source files are then translated to binary, called "binaries", duh

2-programs after that are converted from a human-readable source file
into a machine readable binary
called an executable object
where this process is performed by a compile driver
first the program goes through the preprocessor
where it makes the program ready for compilation
then through the compiler which transforms it to assembly code
then the assember which makes it partitioned binaries
then the linker which puts them all together

